<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Megabazus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Megabazus was a Persian general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> in the late 6th century BCE. Left in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dariuss-scythian-campaign">Darius's Scythian campaign</a>, he conquered Perinthus, much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> and the Paeonians, and secured the submission of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> records his remark that the founders of Chalcedon must have been blind to settle there when the far better site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> lay opposite.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/megabazus.jpg" alt="Megabazus" width="320" height="303" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ekvcpa पाटलिपुत्र · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Achaemenid_lineage_(extended).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
